  partName: Oil Pan
  description: The Oil Pan is a medium-sized, elongated component made of Frame material,
    located at the bottom-center-center of the engine, responsible for storing and
    circulating engine oil. Its size and shape allow it to hold a sufficient amount
    of oil, while its material provides strength and durability. Notably, the Oil
    Pan is designed with a sloping bottom to facilitate oil drainage and maintenance.
